agterm-rs: hosted Wuffs builds (herdr's libghostty-vt patch 0004, rebased onto LIBGHOSTTY_VT_REV)

From herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr, HERDR_REV 143bf5f, Apache-2.0):
vendor/patches/libghostty-vt/0004-fix-hosted-wuffs-builds.patch, modified: its paths rebased off
vendor/libghostty-vt/, and the translator's libc option written for the pin's pkg/translate-c wrapper, whose
`libc_file` is a union (`.direct` or `.detect_darwin`, the default) where herdr's base took a plain path. Without a
--libc file the option stays `.detect_darwin`, so native builds are unchanged. Reason and remove-when:
build/patches/ghostty-vt/README.md.

- pkg/wuffs/build.zig: the build's --libc file (Windows MSVC's SDK) reaches Wuffs' translate-c step, which does not
  inherit it the way the C compiles do;
- pkg/wuffs/src/main.zig: the weak calloc/free stubs are exported for freestanding targets only, so on a hosted
  target with libc unlinked (a build with SIMD off) they never stand in for the embedding executable's libc.

Applied by scripts/build-ghostty-vt.sh. No header changes.

--- a/pkg/wuffs/build.zig
+++ b/pkg/wuffs/build.zig
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@
             .optimize = optimize,
             .include_paths = include_paths,
             .link_libc = windows,
+            // The build's --libc file (an MSVC SDK on Windows) reaches the
+            // C compiles by itself, but the translator needs it explicitly.
+            // Without one, the Darwin SDK is detected as before.
+            .libc_file = if (b.libc_file) |path| .{ .direct = .{ .cwd_relative = path } } else .detect_darwin,
             .extra_args = macro_flags,
         });
 
--- a/pkg/wuffs/src/main.zig
+++ b/pkg/wuffs/src/main.zig
@@ -20,12 +20,11 @@
 // Wuffs' generated `wuffs_foo__bar__alloc()` convenience functions are the
 // only code that references libc's calloc/free. We never call them
 // and linker garbage collection strips them, but that isn't guaranteed.
-// When libc isn't linked there would be nothing to provide calloc/free if
-// they survive, so export stubs to satisfy the link. Weak so that any real
-// definition wins. Hidden keeps them out of the export table where the
-// format honors it (e.g. wasm).
+// Freestanding consumers may have no allocator to resolve these symbols.
+// Never export stubs for hosted targets: hidden weak symbols in a static
+// archive can override the embedding executable's dynamically linked libc.
 comptime {
-    if (!builtin.link_libc) {
+    if (!builtin.link_libc and builtin.os.tag == .freestanding) {
         @export(&callocStub, .{
             .name = "calloc",
             .linkage = .weak,
